# Python & FastAPI Standards

## Style

- Python 3.11+, type hints on public functions and API boundaries
- Format with Ruff/Black conventions; keep imports ordered and unused imports removed
- Prefer `async def` for I/O-bound FastAPI routes and clients
- Use Pydantic v2 models for all request/response/config schemas

## Structure

```
backend/
  app/
    api/           # routers only — thin handlers
    core/          # config, logging, security
    models/        # Pydantic schemas
    services/      # business logic (embed, retrieve, generate)
    pipelines/     # ingest/chunk/index orchestration
    clients/       # Gemini, Pinecone wrappers
  main.py
```

## API rules

```python
# ❌ BAD — fat route with mixed concerns
@app.post("/query")
async def query(q: str):
    emb = genai.embed(q)
    hits = pinecone.query(emb)
    return genai.generate(hits, q)

# ✅ GOOD — thin route, injected service
@router.post("/query", response_model=QueryResponse)
async def query(body: QueryRequest, rag: RagService = Depends(get_rag_service)):
    return await rag.answer(body)
```

## Errors & config

- Use FastAPI `HTTPException` or domain exceptions mapped in handlers
- Load config via `pydantic-settings` from env; validate at startup
- Centralize embedding modality limits (token/page/duration/count caps) in settings — validate uploads against them before embed
- Log with structured context (`request_id`, `doc_id`, `modality`) — never log API keys
